From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dirk=20J=C3=A4ckel?= <github@dirk.jaeckel.name>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:40:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] p2p: `dnsaddr` feature for DNS, so ant can be built without
 hickory

Myotis: the change of https://github.com/freedom-hq/ant/pull/277 (issue #270),
rebased onto b138f6bc074d8c28149017d4e7b1e80db8c67d4d and limited to the vendored
files (the PR's crates/ant-ffi/Cargo.toml, .github/workflows/ci.yml and AGENTS.md
changes are left out). Drop this patch when upstream has merged the PR
(rust/vendor/ant/VENDORED.md, "Patches").

ant-p2p resolves `/dnsaddr/` bootnodes with hickory-resolver 0.25 and
dials `/dns*/` addresses through libp2p's DNS transport, which pins
hickory 0.25 too. Embedders that resolve names themselves, or pass
bootnodes as IP multiaddrs, have no way to leave either out.

Both are now ant-p2p's `dnsaddr` feature, on by default (and forwarded
by ant-node's `dnsaddr`, also default): nothing changes for antd,
ant-ffi or anyone on default features. With it off:

- hickory-resolver and libp2p-dns are not built (the workspace's libp2p
  no longer enables `dns`; `dnsaddr` does);
- the `dnsaddr` module and `default_mainnet_bootnodes()` (a `/dnsaddr/`
  entry) are not compiled;
- a bootnode named by DNS (`/dnsaddr/`, `/dns/`, `/dns4/`, `/dns6/`) is
  refused at start with `RunError::DnsBootnode`, while IP multiaddr
  bootnodes are dialed as given.

ant-ffi, which uses `default_mainnet_bootnodes()` with default features
off, asks for `dnsaddr` explicitly; `cheque_smoke` requires it. CI builds,
lints and tests ant-p2p without the feature and checks that hickory and
libp2p-dns are then not in ant-node's graph on any target.

Closes #270

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
